+        For example, an enterprise customer's sites, connected via a
+        BGP/MPLS VPN <xref target="RFC4364"/> operated by a
+        third-party network provider, may themselves be distributed
+        across different AS domains that are all under the customer's
+        own administration (i.e., the customer's sites form an OAD).
+        In such cases, the customer may want certain attributes
+        relevant to their own VPN routes to be propagated consistently
+        among all of their sites, to influence the BGP decision
+        process at each site.  This does not extend to the internal
+        attributes of the VPN provider's network (e.g., LOCAL_PREF or
+        Route Target values used by the provider), which are not
+        intended to be shared with, or influenced by, the customer's
+        sites.
